message: "If you use this research or its materials, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Evidence-Traceable Verification: Auditing Evidence Traceability in AI Fact-Checking"
authors:
  - family-names: Celik
    given-names: Hazal
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
type: research
abstract: >-
  This research audits evidence traceability in AI fact-checking records
  using AVeriTeC as a case study. It examines six dimensions of evidence
  documentation and proposes the Evidence-Traceable Verification Model
  (ETVM) as a framework for more transparent and auditable verification.
repository-code: "https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/evidence-traceable-verification"

